List the sources Knapsack installs addons from, choose how each is read,
and manage their API keys.

CurseForge and Wago are read from their websites by default, as a browser
reads them, which needs no key. Their official APIs give keys out only to
some; with one, `knapsack sources set-api <source> official` reads the API
instead. The website isn't an API, so it can change under Knapsack: when
it does, the error has a link to report it.

Keys are shared by every profile. They're stored in config.toml, which is
then readable only by you, and an environment variable overrides each one
(KNAPSACK_CURSEFORGE_API_KEY, KNAPSACK_WAGO_API_KEY), so a config kept in a
dotfiles repo can leave them out. GitHub needs no key: Knapsack uses a token
from GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN or the GitHub CLI when there is one, for a
higher rate limit, and never stores it.

Usage:
  knapsack sources [flags]
  knapsack sources [command]

Available Commands:
  list        List sources, how each is read, and whether it's ready
  set-api     Choose whether a source is read from its website or its official API
  set-key     Store a source's API key
  unset-key   Remove a source's API key from config

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for sources

Global Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors

Use "knapsack sources [command] --help" for more information about a command.
